{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1562001-anne-rice-s-immortal-universe-rpg","id":1562001,"title":"Anne Rice's Immortal Universe RPG","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-07-21T10:14:35-07:00","id":1562001,"title":"Anne Rice's Immortal Universe RPG","content":"Well, it's finally happening. Renegade Games, the ones who made the current editions of Vampire: The Masquerade, Hunter: The Reckoning, and Werewolf: The Apocalypse, is going to make a RPG based on Anne Rice's novels. They are calling it the Immortal Universe. Link to article below. What do you think?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://renegadegamestudios.com/blog/renegade-game-studios-and-amc-global-media-announceanne-rices-immortal-universeroleplaying-game/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-kftzvkkgjv/product_images/uploaded_images/screenshot-2026-07-20-at-2.55.41-pm.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://renegadegamestudios.com/blog/renegade-game-studios-and-amc-global-media-announceanne-rices-immortal-universeroleplaying-game/\" target=\"_blank\"> Renegade Game Studios and AMC Global Media Announce&nbsp;Anne Rice's Immortal Universe&nbsp;Roleplaying Game </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://renegadegamestudios.com/blog/renegade-game-studios-and-amc-global-media-announceanne-rices-immortal-universeroleplaying-game/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://renegadegamestudios.com/blog/renegade-game-studios-and-amc-global-media-announceanne-rices-immortal-universeroleplaying-game/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Renegade Game Studios and AMC Global Media Announce&amp;nbsp;Anne Rice's Immortal Universe&amp;nbsp;Roleplaying Game Renegade is partnering with AMC to produce TTRPG titles for hit television series including Anne Rice&amp;rsquo;s Interview with the Vampire, Anne Rice&amp;rsquo;s Mayfair Witches, and more&amp;hellip; Step into the world of Anne Rice's Immortal Universe, AMC&amp;rsquo;s acclaimed original franchise based on the beloved book series, in an all-new tabletop roleplaying game where relationships matter more than power, memory is as dangerous as any monster, and every choice echoes across generations. Create your own stories of vampires, witches, psychics, and ordinary humans whose lives become forever entwined through love, loyalty, ambition, and loss. Together, you'll build chronicles that span decades, or centuries, exploring the emotional consequences and impossible choices of immortality. This is a gothic horror RPG where the greatest monsters are often our own desires. A Different Kind of Supernatural Roleplaying Game While many supernatural RPGs focus on the struggle for power, political intrigue, and territorial conflict, Anne Rice's Immortal Universe Roleplaying Game tells stories about relationships. Family. Devotion. Betrayal. Loneliness. Memory. The greatest threat is never simply an enemy across the table&amp;hellip; often, it&amp;rsquo;s someone you can&amp;rsquo;t let go. Every decision carries emotional weight, and every relationship has the potential to reshape the world. Stories Across the Ages Anne Rice&amp;rsquo;s Immortal Universe isn't confined to a single moment in history. You will build chronicles that move between modern nights and forgotten decades. Follow characters whose histories stretch across lifetimes and eras. Discover how ancient promises, old betrayals, and memories long buried continue to shape the present. In this world, the past is never truly gone. A Storytelling System Designed for Anne Rice's Immortal Universe The game's mechanics are built to reinforce the themes that define Anne Rice's stories featured in the hit television series: Success can be as dramatic as failure. Even when characters achieve exactly what they desire, victory may create unforeseen complications, heartbreak, or tragedy. Flashbacks reshape the present. Using the game's Flashback System, players revisit moments from their characters' pasts, from brief interludes to entire sessions, revealing new truths that can transform the current story. Time is a river, but you can fly. A chronicle might begin in modern-day New Orleans before traveling back to Paris in the 1800s, revealing events that forever change what players thought they knew. The past is a mechanic. Memory, unreliable narration, and personal history are woven directly into gameplay, making history an active part of every session rather than mere background lore. Collaborative storytelling. Through the game's Rewrite&amp;nbsp;mechanic, players may gain opportunities to briefly gain narrative control, deeply influencing scenes as they unfold and helping to shape dramatic moments. Three damage tracks represent physical, psychological, and emotional harm, ensuring the consequences of every encounter extend beyond simple injury. Healing comes through identity. Recovery isn't just about resting; instead, it comes from embracing who your character truly is. The more authentically you play your character, the more you&amp;rsquo;ll heal your mind and body. Coming to BackerKit in Fall 2026 The Anne Rice&amp;rsquo;s Immortal Universe RPG debuts with a journey into the themes and setting of AMC&amp;rsquo;s Interview with the Vampire, coming to BackerKit this Fall. This crowdfunding campaign will introduce the first chapter of the Anne Rice's Immortal Universe Roleplaying Game, inviting players to explore the world that began with Louis, Lestat, Claudia, and the unforgettable city of New Orleans. The campaign will feature: Anne Rice&amp;rsquo;s Immortal Universe Roleplaying Game: Interview with the Vampire Starter Set Interview with the Vampire: New Orleans Rulebook Premium accessories, including liquid core dice, character journals, dice bags, and more. Campaign exclusive collectibles available only during the BackerKit campaign. But this is only the beginning. Interview with the Vampire is the first entry in a connected roleplaying game line inspired by Anne Rice's Immortal Universe. Future releases will expand beyond humans and vampires, introducing witches, psychics, and other corners of this supernatural world, allowing players to build stories that delve into every lush nook and cranny of the Immortal Universe. So&amp;hellip; will you join us? Follow the Campaign </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T13:21:24-07:00","id":1562005,"title":"","content":"Hope goes well, but won't bet on it.<br /> <br /> Their track record with Vampire, Hunter and Werewolf is itself a reason to be wary of this. Their work with Vampire is ok-ish, with Hunter is very weak and with Werewolf is atrocious.<br /> <br /> And this isn't based in the novels. This is based in the series based in the novels. That's a <u><b>BIG</b></u> difference.<br /> <br /> Finally, I find RPGs based in franchises always a hard sell. Not only is it hard to hit the notes people expect, when they do they frequently end up being rather weak as TTRPGs because the source material isn't really good for that. An RPG setting has very different requirements from a regular media franchise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T22:56:16-07:00","id":1562029,"title":"","content":"You know it would be really funny if Renegades Immortal Universe werewolf game consists of even more materials from the cancelled version of W5 to the point it's more werewolf the apocalypse game than proper W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T01:28:21-07:00","id":1562035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1562001-anne-rice-s-immortal-universe-rpg?p=1562029#post1562029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know it would be really funny if Renegades Immortal Universe werewolf game consists of even more materials from the cancelled version of W5 to the point it's more werewolf the apocalypse game than proper W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's even relevant to be brought up. Don't think it will be a series of gamelines either, seems it will rather be a unified setting and supplements.<br /> <br /> Also wouldn't be surprised if they prioritize the creatures that actually appeared in the series: witches and psychics. After that, if they go to the books, even the aliens and homunculi are more likely to come first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T04:24:02-07:00","id":1562040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1562001-anne-rice-s-immortal-universe-rpg?p=1562005#post1562005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this isn't based in the novels. This is based in the series based in the novels. That's a <u><b>BIG</b></u> difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, it's weird with as much material as the novels have, that it wouldn't be more based on the books than the series. I mean, I get why they'd want to hook in people who watch the show, but anyone who might actually play this game has probably read a lot of the books as well.<br /> <br /> But, we'll see what they do with it....<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> ________________