2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T15:58:12-07:00","id":1562064,"title":"","content":"The AMC-not-estate detail explains a lot, and honestly the mechanics they teased are more interesting to me than the branding. A flashback system, three separate tracks for physical/psychological/emotional harm, and healing through authentically playing your character is a genuinely Rice-flavored design goal, even if it comes via the show. That's a much better fit for her material than bolting it onto a power-and-territory engine. I share monteparnas' skepticism given the track record, but I'd rather they swing for the emotional stuff and miss than play it safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29129-daria22","name":"daria22","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T17:51:38-07:00","id":1562066,"title":"","content":"O agree.<br /> <br /> The part of going for relationships gives me serious MonsterHearts vibes, and that's a very good indie TTRPG, so I really want this to go well.<br /> <br /> And if they genuinely try and miss, my respect for them will grow nonetheless. Again, risking to tackle hard questions rather than pretend they don't exist is what made WoD and CoD into what they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-26T05:26:05-07:00","id":1562179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1562001-anne-rice-s-immortal-universe-rpg?p=1562041#post1562041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not, is a partnership with the show runners, not with Rice's estate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh.. well, that explains it then.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>daria22</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1562001-anne-rice-s-immortal-universe-rpg?p=1562064#post1562064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The AMC-not-estate detail explains a lot, and honestly the mechanics they teased are more interesting to me than the branding. A flashback system, three separate tracks for physical/psychological/emotional harm, and healing through authentically playing your character is a genuinely Rice-flavored design goal, even if it comes via the show. That's a much better fit for her material than bolting it onto a power-and-territory engine. I share monteparnas' skepticism given the track record, but I'd rather they swing for the emotional stuff and miss than play it safe.</div> </div> </div> </div>In theory it sounds like it could make for an interesting game...hopefully they can do something cool with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T20:39:24-07:00","id":1562610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1562001-anne-rice-s-immortal-universe-rpg?p=1562005#post1562005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hope goes well, but won't bet on it.<br /> <br /> Their track record with Vampire, Hunter and Werewolf is itself a reason to be wary of this. Their work with Vampire is ok-ish, with Hunter is very weak and with Werewolf is atrocious.<br /> <br /> And this isn't based in the novels. This is based in the series based in the novels. That's a <u><b>BIG</b></u> difference.<br /> <br /> Finally, I find RPGs based in franchises always a hard sell. Not only is it hard to hit the notes people expect, when they do they frequently end up being rather weak as TTRPGs because the source material isn't really good for that. An RPG setting has very different requirements from a regular media franchise.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mention of a flashback system sounds like it could be a recipe for disaster.<br /> <br /> Either it risks the players creating a time paradox by disrupting events that are destined to happen in the future.<br /> <br /> OR, it makes the session / scene boring, because you already know how events unfolded, and you're just retreading the same steps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T22:33:37-07:00","id":1562614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1562001-anne-rice-s-immortal-universe-rpg?p=1562610#post1562610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mention of a flashback system sounds like it could be a recipe for disaster.<br /> <br /> Either it risks the players creating a time paradox by disrupting events that are destined to happen in the future.<br /> <br /> OR, it makes the session / scene boring, because you already know how events unfolded, and you're just retreading the same steps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily, only if the result of the flashback impacts something already defined in the story.<br /> <br /> Let's say the flashback refers to the first time you met an NPC. We have roughly three cases:<br /> <br /> 1. The NPC has appeared in the chronicle in the present already. That means we already have an established relationship between the two characters.<br /> <br /> 2. The NPC didn't appeared yet, only the fact you met before is established.<br /> <br /> 3. The NPC appeared, but the first time you met was a long time ago.<br /> <br /> Number 1 is a problem for the reasons you said, but not the other two. Number 2 is a way to define how the two characters relate before they meet in the present, it's relatively free. And number 3 has a time gap that can explain any inconsistency: whatever is different changed in the meantime.<br /> <br /> Will it work? Idk. Renegade Studios doesn't inspire me confidence. But at least they're working with a material that's more their thing: a setting focused on Europe and the US where you're not required to deal with minorities. You can do, as they did in <i>Interview</i>, but don't have to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T22:54:59-07:00","id":1562616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1562001-anne-rice-s-immortal-universe-rpg?p=1562614#post1562614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not necessarily, only if the result of the flashback impacts something already defined in the story.<br /> <br /> Let's say the flashback refers to the first time you met an NPC. We have roughly three cases:<br /> <br /> 1. The NPC has appeared in the chronicle in the present already. That means we already have an established relationship between the two characters.<br /> <br /> 2. The NPC didn't appeared yet, only the fact you met before is established.<br /> <br /> 3. The NPC appeared, but the first time you met was a long time ago.<br /> <br /> Number 1 is a problem for the reasons you said, but not the other two. Number 2 is a way to define how the two characters relate before they meet in the present, it's relatively free. And number 3 has a time gap that can explain any inconsistency: whatever is different changed in the meantime.<br /> <br /> Will it work? Idk. Renegade Studios doesn't inspire me confidence. But at least they're working with a material that's more their thing: a setting focused on Europe and the US where you're not required to deal with minorities. You can do, as they did in <i>Interview</i>, but don't have to.</div> </div> </div> </div>That third example sounds more like a memory, than a proper recap. Events being hazy or unreliable, due to the character not having a clear picture.<br /> <br /> Which could have the potential for an interesting story element, assuming that both the player and whatever equates to a GM cooperate with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkk